  [("val", "Property value ($)", 400000), ("loan", "Loan balance ($)", 300000)],
  r"""const l=loan/val*100;return [['Loan-to-value',PCT(l,2)],['Equity',M(val-loan)],['PMI likely?',l>80?'Yes, above 80% LTV':'No, at or under 80%']];""",
  "LTV = loan balance / property value. Lenders use it to price risk. PMI is typically required above 80%.",
